    <detaileddescription>
<para>Welcome to the engineering manual for the <bold>CloudAvid File Portal</bold>: a zero-framework, filesystem-driven download portal with a Single Page Application (SPA) frontend and a two-layer Node.js back-end.</para>
<para>─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────</para>
<sect1 id="index_1manual_overview">
<title>📖 Overview: The Portal in One Paragraph</title><para><simplesect kind="par"><title>🧒 ELI5</title><para>The portal is a <bold>library</bold>. Two pretty rooms — <computeroutput><ref refid="index_8html" kindref="compound">index.html</ref></computeroutput> and <computeroutput><ref refid="browse_8html" kindref="compound">browse.html</ref></computeroutput> — are where visitors stand. A helpful clerk (<computeroutput><ref refid="resource-service_8js_source" kindref="compound">assets/js/services/resource-service.js</ref></computeroutput>) takes the visitor&apos;s requests to the front desk (<computeroutput><ref refid="server_8js" kindref="compound">server.js</ref></computeroutput>), and the front desk calls the basement keeper (<computeroutput><ref refid="files-service_8js" kindref="compound">lib/files-service.js</ref></computeroutput>), the only person with the key to the storage room (<computeroutput>FILES_ROOT</computeroutput>). Nobody skips a layer: visitors never walk into the basement, and the basement keeper never talks to visitors directly.</para>
</simplesect>
<simplesect kind="par"><title>🧭 The Two-Layer Rule (the project&apos;s most important convention)</title><para>All communication flows through exactly one HTTP seam (<computeroutput><ref refid="resource-service_8js_source" kindref="compound">assets/js/services/resource-service.js</ref></computeroutput> → <computeroutput><ref refid="server_8js" kindref="compound">server.js</ref></computeroutput> → <computeroutput><ref refid="files-service_8js" kindref="compound">lib/files-service.js</ref></computeroutput>). Each layer is deliberately blind to the others&apos; internals:</para>
</simplesect>
<table rows="6" cols="4"><row>
<entry thead="yes"><para>Layer  </para>
</entry><entry thead="yes"><para>Files  </para>
</entry><entry thead="yes"><para>Allowed to do  </para>
</entry><entry thead="yes"><para>Forbidden to do  </para>
</entry></row>
<row>
<entry thead="no"><para><bold>Shell</bold>  </para>
</entry><entry thead="no"><para><computeroutput><ref refid="index_8html" kindref="compound">index.html</ref></computeroutput>, <computeroutput><ref refid="browse_8html" kindref="compound">browse.html</ref></computeroutput>  </para>
</entry><entry thead="no"><para>Persistent chrome (navbar/footer), asset pipeline, <computeroutput>&lt;main id="app"&gt;</computeroutput> mount point  </para>
</entry><entry thead="no"><para>Contain business logic  </para>
</entry></row>
<row>
<entry thead="no"><para><bold>View / Router</bold>  </para>
</entry><entry thead="no"><para><computeroutput><ref refid="router_8js_source" kindref="compound">assets/js/router.js</ref></computeroutput>, <computeroutput><ref refid="home_8js_source" kindref="compound">home.js</ref></computeroutput>, <computeroutput><ref refid="browse_8js_source" kindref="compound">browse.js</ref></computeroutput>, <computeroutput><ref refid="autocomplete_8js_source" kindref="compound">autocomplete.js</ref></computeroutput>  </para>
</entry><entry thead="no"><para>Render views, react to input  </para>
</entry><entry thead="no"><para>Fetch the API directly (must go through the service layer)  </para>
</entry></row>
<row>
<entry thead="no"><para><bold>Data service</bold>  </para>
</entry><entry thead="no"><para><computeroutput><ref refid="resource-service_8js_source" kindref="compound">assets/js/services/resource-service.js</ref></computeroutput>  </para>
</entry><entry thead="no"><para>All <computeroutput>fetch("/api/…")</computeroutput> calls, sessionStorage cache (5 min TTL), URL building (<computeroutput>browseHref</computeroutput>/<computeroutput>downloadHref</computeroutput>)  </para>
</entry><entry thead="no"><para>Touch the DOM  </para>
</entry></row>
<row>
<entry thead="no"><para><bold>HTTP transport</bold>  </para>
</entry><entry thead="no"><para><computeroutput><ref refid="server_8js" kindref="compound">server.js</ref></computeroutput>  </para>
</entry><entry thead="no"><para>Routing, headers, CORS, MIME, streaming, security blocklist (<computeroutput>/.env</computeroutput>, <computeroutput>/lib/</computeroutput>, <computeroutput>/node_modules/</computeroutput>)  </para>
</entry><entry thead="no"><para>Any filesystem decision-making  </para>
</entry></row>
<row>
<entry thead="no"><para><bold>Filesystem domain</bold>  </para>
</entry><entry thead="no"><para><computeroutput><ref refid="files-service_8js" kindref="compound">lib/files-service.js</ref></computeroutput>  </para>
</entry><entry thead="no"><para>FILES_ROOT resolution, path-safety wall, directory walks, search, release ranking  </para>
</entry><entry thead="no"><para>Write headers, see request objects, stream bytes  </para>
</entry></row>
</table>
</para>
<para>─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────</para>
</sect1>
