<sect1 id="index_1manual_toc">
<title>🧭 Reading Order</title><para>The manual has four chapters. Each chapter page summarises one documented file and links into its full documentation. Read top to bottom for the intended learning path — shell first, then the wire, then the disk:</para>
<para><orderedlist>
<listitem><para><bold><ref refid="chap_index" kindref="compound">Chapter 1 — index.html: The SPA Shell</ref></bold> — the SPA shell: pre-paint boot, theme and performance tiers, the <computeroutput>#app</computeroutput> mount point, and the ordered script pipeline. <emphasis>Start here: everything the user sees loads through it.</emphasis></para>
</listitem><listitem><para><bold><ref refid="chap_browse" kindref="compound">Chapter 2 — browse.html: The Deep-Link Shell</ref></bold> — the deep-link shell for <computeroutput>/browse/…</computeroutput> routes, so a refresh or shared link inside the catalogue still boots the same SPA.</para>
</listitem><listitem><para><bold><ref refid="chap_server" kindref="compound">Chapter 3 — server.js: The HTTP Transport Layer</ref></bold> — the HTTP transport: every route, the security blocklist, streaming downloads, and the error funnel.</para>
</listitem><listitem><para><bold><ref refid="chap_files" kindref="compound">Chapter 4 — lib/files-service.js: The Filesystem Domain Layer</ref></bold> — the filesystem domain layer: FILES_ROOT validation, the path-safety wall, and the three tree walkers.</para>
</listitem></orderedlist>
</para>
