<sect1 id="index_1manual_api">
<title>📡 The JSON API Surface (one table)</title><para>All six routes live in <computeroutput><ref refid="server_8js" kindref="compound">server.js</ref></computeroutput> and delegate every filesystem decision to <computeroutput><ref refid="files-service_8js" kindref="compound">lib/files-service.js</ref></computeroutput>. The browser reaches them only through <computeroutput><ref refid="resource-service_8js_source" kindref="compound">resource-service.js</ref></computeroutput> (directly, or via <computeroutput>nginx.conf</computeroutput> in production).</para>
<para><table rows="7" cols="4"><row>
<entry thead="yes"><para>Route  </para>
</entry><entry thead="yes"><para><ref refid="server_8js" kindref="compound">server.js</ref> handler  </para>
</entry><entry thead="yes"><para><ref refid="files-service_8js" kindref="compound">files-service.js</ref> call  </para>
</entry><entry thead="yes"><para>Frontend caller  </para>
</entry></row>
<row>
<entry thead="no"><para><computeroutput>GET /__health</computeroutput>, <computeroutput>GET /api/health</computeroutput>  </para>
</entry><entry thead="no"><para>inline  </para>
</entry><entry thead="no"><para><computeroutput>peekRootSync()</computeroutput>  </para>
</entry><entry thead="no"><para>uptime monitors  </para>
</entry></row>
<row>
<entry thead="no"><para><computeroutput>GET /api/categories</computeroutput>  </para>
</entry><entry thead="no"><para>inline  </para>
</entry><entry thead="no"><para><computeroutput>listCategories()</computeroutput>  </para>
</entry><entry thead="no"><para><computeroutput>getResources()</computeroutput> → <computeroutput><ref refid="home_8js_source" kindref="compound">home.js</ref></computeroutput> cards  </para>
</entry></row>
<row>
<entry thead="no"><para><computeroutput>GET /api/releases?limit=</computeroutput>  </para>
</entry><entry thead="no"><para>inline  </para>
</entry><entry thead="no"><para><computeroutput>listLatestReleases()</computeroutput>  </para>
</entry><entry thead="no"><para><computeroutput>getReleases()</computeroutput> → <computeroutput><ref refid="home_8js_source" kindref="compound">home.js</ref></computeroutput>  </para>
</entry></row>
<row>
<entry thead="no"><para><computeroutput>GET /api/search?q=&amp;limit=</computeroutput>  </para>
</entry><entry thead="no"><para>inline  </para>
</entry><entry thead="no"><para><computeroutput>searchEntries()</computeroutput>  </para>
</entry><entry thead="no"><para><computeroutput>search()</computeroutput> → <computeroutput><ref refid="autocomplete_8js_source" kindref="compound">autocomplete.js</ref></computeroutput>, <computeroutput><ref refid="home_8js_source" kindref="compound">home.js</ref></computeroutput>  </para>
</entry></row>
<row>
<entry thead="no"><para><computeroutput>GET /api/files[/&lt;rel&gt;]</computeroutput>, <computeroutput>?path=</computeroutput>  </para>
</entry><entry thead="no"><para>inline  </para>
</entry><entry thead="no"><para><computeroutput>listPath()</computeroutput>  </para>
</entry><entry thead="no"><para><computeroutput>listFiles()</computeroutput> → <computeroutput><ref refid="browse_8js_source" kindref="compound">browse.js</ref></computeroutput>  </para>
</entry></row>
<row>
<entry thead="no"><para><computeroutput>GET/HEAD /api/download[/&lt;rel&gt;]</computeroutput>, <computeroutput>?path=</computeroutput>  </para>
</entry><entry thead="no"><para><computeroutput>streamDownload()</computeroutput>  </para>
</entry><entry thead="no"><para><computeroutput>getDownloadTarget()</computeroutput>  </para>
</entry><entry thead="no"><para><computeroutput>downloadHref()</computeroutput> → <computeroutput><ref refid="browse_8js_source" kindref="compound">browse.js</ref></computeroutput>, <computeroutput><ref refid="home_8js_source" kindref="compound">home.js</ref></computeroutput>, <computeroutput><ref refid="autocomplete_8js_source" kindref="compound">autocomplete.js</ref></computeroutput>  </para>
</entry></row>
</table>
</para>
<para>Non-API routes: <computeroutput>/</computeroutput>, <computeroutput>/index.html</computeroutput>, <computeroutput>/browse</computeroutput> and <computeroutput>/browse/…</computeroutput> serve the SPA shell (<computeroutput>serveSPA</computeroutput>); everything else is static assets via <computeroutput>serveStatic</computeroutput>, with a hard 403 on <computeroutput>/.env</computeroutput>, <computeroutput>/lib/</computeroutput>, <computeroutput>/node_modules/</computeroutput>.</para>
<para>─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────</para>
</sect1>
<sect1 id="index_1manual_errors">
<title>🚨 The Shared Error Contract</title><para>Every back-end failure is created by <computeroutput>serviceError()</computeroutput> in <computeroutput><ref refid="files-service_8js" kindref="compound">lib/files-service.js</ref></computeroutput> and rendered verbatim by <computeroutput>sendServiceError()</computeroutput> in <computeroutput><ref refid="server_8js" kindref="compound">server.js</ref></computeroutput> as <computeroutput>{ "error": &lt;message&gt;, "code": &lt;code&gt; }</computeroutput>. These codes are a public contract — the frontend surfaces them and operators match on them:</para>
<para><table rows="11" cols="4"><row>
<entry thead="yes"><para>Code  </para>
</entry><entry thead="yes"><para>HTTP  </para>
</entry><entry thead="yes"><para>Thrown by  </para>
</entry><entry thead="yes"><para>Meaning  </para>
</entry></row>
<row>
<entry thead="no"><para><computeroutput>FILES_ROOT_MISSING</computeroutput>  </para>
</entry><entry thead="no"><para>503  </para>
</entry><entry thead="no"><para><computeroutput>resolveConfiguredRoot()</computeroutput>  </para>
</entry><entry thead="no"><para><computeroutput>FILES_ROOT</computeroutput> unset or blank in <computeroutput>.env</computeroutput>  </para>
</entry></row>
<row>
<entry thead="no"><para><computeroutput>FILES_ROOT_NOT_FOUND</computeroutput>  </para>
</entry><entry thead="no"><para>503  </para>
</entry><entry thead="no"><para><computeroutput>getRoot()</computeroutput>  </para>
</entry><entry thead="no"><para>Configured path does not exist  </para>
</entry></row>
<row>
<entry thead="no"><para><computeroutput>FILES_ROOT_NOT_DIRECTORY</computeroutput>  </para>
</entry><entry thead="no"><para>503  </para>
</entry><entry thead="no"><para><computeroutput>getRoot()</computeroutput>  </para>
</entry><entry thead="no"><para>Configured path is not a directory  </para>
</entry></row>
<row>
<entry thead="no"><para><computeroutput>FILES_ROOT_EMPTY</computeroutput>  </para>
</entry><entry thead="no"><para>503  </para>
</entry><entry thead="no"><para><computeroutput>assertCategoryStructure()</computeroutput>  </para>
</entry><entry thead="no"><para>No visible entries at all  </para>
</entry></row>
<row>
<entry thead="no"><para><computeroutput>FILES_ROOT_NO_CATEGORIES</computeroutput>  </para>
</entry><entry thead="no"><para>503  </para>
</entry><entry thead="no"><para><computeroutput>assertCategoryStructure()</computeroutput>  </para>
</entry><entry thead="no"><para>Only files at root; directories are categories  </para>
</entry></row>
<row>
<entry thead="no"><para><computeroutput>INVALID_PATH</computeroutput>  </para>
</entry><entry thead="no"><para>400  </para>
</entry><entry thead="no"><para><computeroutput>resolveInsideRoot()</computeroutput>, <computeroutput>getDownloadTarget()</computeroutput>  </para>
</entry><entry thead="no"><para><computeroutput>.</computeroutput> / <computeroutput>..</computeroutput> / NUL segment, or blank download path  </para>
</entry></row>
<row>
<entry thead="no"><para><computeroutput>PATH_TRAVERSAL</computeroutput>  </para>
</entry><entry thead="no"><para>403  </para>
</entry><entry thead="no"><para><computeroutput>resolveInsideRoot()</computeroutput>  </para>
</entry><entry thead="no"><para>Resolved target escapes <computeroutput>FILES_ROOT</computeroutput>  </para>
</entry></row>
<row>
<entry thead="no"><para><computeroutput>NOT_FOUND</computeroutput>  </para>
</entry><entry thead="no"><para>404  </para>
</entry><entry thead="no"><para><computeroutput>listPath()</computeroutput>, <computeroutput>getDownloadTarget()</computeroutput>  </para>
</entry><entry thead="no"><para>Target does not exist  </para>
</entry></row>
<row>
<entry thead="no"><para><computeroutput>NOT_A_DIRECTORY</computeroutput>  </para>
</entry><entry thead="no"><para>400  </para>
</entry><entry thead="no"><para><computeroutput>listPath()</computeroutput>  </para>
</entry><entry thead="no"><para>Asked to list a file  </para>
</entry></row>
<row>
<entry thead="no"><para><computeroutput>NOT_A_FILE</computeroutput>  </para>
</entry><entry thead="no"><para>400  </para>
</entry><entry thead="no"><para><computeroutput>getDownloadTarget()</computeroutput>  </para>
</entry><entry thead="no"><para>Asked to download a directory  </para>
</entry></row>
</table>
</para>
<para>─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────</para>
</sect1>
<sect1 id="index_1manual_conventions">
<title>📐 House Conventions (applies to all chapters)</title><para><itemizedlist>
<listitem><para><bold>Module banners:</bold> every source file opens with the <computeroutput>═══</computeroutput> banner comment naming the file and its role.</para>
</listitem><listitem><para><bold>Live documentation:</bold> the <computeroutput>.dox</computeroutput> pages never hardcode source; they inject it with <computeroutput>@snippet &lt;file&gt; &lt;snippet_id&gt;</computeroutput> against <computeroutput>[snippet_id]</computeroutput> marker comments in the sources (see <computeroutput>dox/main/files-service.dox</computeroutput> and the <computeroutput>fs_snip_*</computeroutput> markers in <computeroutput><ref refid="files-service_8js" kindref="compound">lib/files-service.js</ref></computeroutput>).</para>
</listitem><listitem><para><bold>Hybrid tone:</bold> ELI5 analogies for <emphasis>what/why</emphasis>, senior depth for <emphasis>how</emphasis>, plus a ⚠️ breaking-change warning per logical block.</para>
</listitem><listitem><para><bold>Diagrams:</bold> Graphviz <computeroutput>@dot</computeroutput> with the pastel palette (<computeroutput>#DBEAFE</computeroutput> entry · <computeroutput>#FEF3C7</computeroutput> processing · <computeroutput>#D1FAE5</computeroutput> output · <computeroutput>#FCE7F3</computeroutput> side-effects · <computeroutput>#E0E7FF</computeroutput> external · <computeroutput>#FFEDD5</computeroutput> storage); PlantUML <computeroutput>@startuml</computeroutput> for interaction timelines.</para>
</listitem><listitem><para><bold>Hidden-entry rule:</bold> <computeroutput><ref refid="index_8html" kindref="compound">index.html</ref></computeroutput>, <computeroutput>index.php</computeroutput> and dotfiles never appear in listings. The authoritative filter is <computeroutput>isHidden()</computeroutput> in <computeroutput><ref refid="files-service_8js" kindref="compound">lib/files-service.js</ref></computeroutput>; <computeroutput><ref refid="browse_8js_source" kindref="compound">browse.js</ref></computeroutput> and <computeroutput><ref refid="resource-service_8js_source" kindref="compound">resource-service.js</ref></computeroutput> keep defensive display-level copies.</para>
</listitem><listitem><para><bold>Caching:</bold> the API never caches (<computeroutput>Cache-Control: no-store</computeroutput>); the only cache is the browser&apos;s sessionStorage TTL in <computeroutput><ref refid="resource-service_8js_source" kindref="compound">resource-service.js</ref></computeroutput>.</para>
</listitem><listitem><para><bold>Config:</bold> no hardcoded paths — <computeroutput>PORT</computeroutput> and <computeroutput>FILES_ROOT</computeroutput> come from <computeroutput>.env</computeroutput> via <computeroutput><ref refid="load-env_8js_source" kindref="compound">lib/load-env.js</ref></computeroutput> (template: <computeroutput>.env.example</computeroutput>).</para>
</listitem></itemizedlist>
</para>
</sect1>
